From a6a56f6a97c4fd3f1e0b4c6864b500d86af8e3b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:45:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] server: add --spec-grammar to draft for grammar-constrained
 requests

The 2026-09-15 guard (3e7b73528) turns speculative decoding off for any
request with a grammar, which leaves tool-call traffic on plain decode.
--spec-grammar (env LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_GRAMMAR) lifts it; the default keeps
the guard. Synthetic acceptance keeps the guard and warns, since it takes
draft tokens without the grammar.

The verify path already keeps grammar output exact: each position is
sampled through the grammar and accepted before the next is checked, and
a checkpoint restore copies the whole sampler back. The corruption the
guard was added for came from the SSM_CONV_SPLIT conv-state bug (added
7f64d1946 the day before, fixed 0359ec5d4 on 2026-09-24), which corrupted
the state on every multi-token verify ubatch. FLEET.md has the story in
one entry, with the CPU A/B.

Tests: test-sampler-copy-grammar (common_sampler_copy restores a lazy
grammar's trigger state and buffer, and the reasoning-budget state), a
server test that greedy output under a grammar is unchanged with drafting
on, and an opt-in server test (LLAMA_TEST_HYBRID_MODEL) that counts
checkpoint restores under a grammar on a qwen35 model. Adds
tools/server/bench/spec_grammar_stress.py, a tool-call validity and speed
A/B to run with and without the flag.

